# modules/keys/env.schema — KEY=description:required|optional
VAULTWARDEN_MODE=tunnel | mesh_only — how vault.<domain> is published (§2.2):required
VAULTWARDEN_DOMAIN=Full origin Vaultwarden advertises to clients (https://vault.<domain>):required
EVENTS_DAYS_RETAIN=Days of Vaultwarden org events kept for SENT-K-* and REQ-028 (default 1095):required
POSTGRES_USER=Shared Postgres user; Vaultwarden uses the separate vaultwarden database (Decision 19):required
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=Shared Postgres password:required
SENTINEL_DATA_DIR=Host data root; supplies /certs (wildcard) and the maintenance-mode marker dir:required
MESH_BIND_IP=Mesh interface IP for the :443 mesh-side listener:required
SMTP_HOST=Firm SMTP relay host (invites, password hints, 2FA mail):required
SMTP_PORT=SMTP port:required
SMTP_USERNAME=SMTP username:optional
SMTP_FROM=From address on Vaultwarden mail:required
ADMIN_TOKEN=DELIBERATELY UNSET at rest. Only maintenance-mode.sh sets it (argon2 hash) for 30 minutes with a change record and an auto-revert:optional
ROCKET_TLS=mesh_only mode only — {certs="/certs/live/wildcard.crt",key="/certs/live/wildcard.key"}. Leave unset in tunnel mode so cloudflared can reach the HTTP origin:optional
